WEBVTT

00:05.640 --> 00:07.230
But what is this?

00:07.230 --> 00:10.230
The school seems different than usual.

00:10.230 --> 00:12.390
Everyone’s kind of anxious, somehow.

00:12.390 --> 00:16.700
Oh, right. Is it because semester finals are coming up?

00:16.700 --> 00:19.220
I need to study, too...

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

01:52.510 --> 01:56.890
I can’t believe we were in tropical Palau just yesterday.

01:57.450 --> 02:00.160
It’s the middle of winter here.

02:00.160 --> 02:00.830
But...

02:02.280 --> 02:07.770
The sweater you knitted for me keeps me
from from being cold at all.

02:08.930 --> 02:10.940
It’s very warm.

02:16.650 --> 02:17.370
Ayako-san?

02:18.810 --> 02:21.220
Y-Yeah, you’re right, Mamoru.

02:21.220 --> 02:24.220
Ayako-san, were you listening?

02:24.970 --> 02:26.800
Of course I was!

02:26.800 --> 02:27.560
But...

02:27.560 --> 02:28.630
It’s nothing.

02:28.630 --> 02:30.560
OK, do your best in class.

02:33.690 --> 02:34.990
Ayako-san?

02:35.600 --> 02:40.600
Sparks Fly on Valentine’s

02:42.930 --> 02:45.970
<i>What’s wrong with Ayako-san?</i>

02:46.430 --> 02:49.410
<i>We were together during the whole trip.</i>

02:55.210 --> 02:57.950
<i>But this morning, she was...</i>

03:00.840 --> 03:02.510
<i>What’s wrong?</i>

03:02.510 --> 03:04.100
<i>Did something happen?</i>

03:04.100 --> 03:06.160
Mamoru-kun, is something wrong?

03:07.290 --> 03:08.320
Mitsuki-san.

03:08.320 --> 03:10.390
What, still jet-lagged?

03:10.390 --> 03:12.350
No, that’s not it.

03:12.350 --> 03:13.580
Just...

03:13.580 --> 03:18.260
This morning, Ayako-san was acting
kind of weird, wasn’t she?

03:18.600 --> 03:21.220
Like she wasn’t really here...

03:24.240 --> 03:25.510
Oh, Ayako-san!

03:26.430 --> 03:30.550
Well, it’s really close, isn’t it?

03:34.850 --> 03:37.320
Lunchtime!

03:39.930 --> 03:42.500
<i>What’s really close, I wonder.</i>

03:49.530 --> 03:50.810
Emelenzia!

03:52.080 --> 03:54.630
Are you going to eat, too?

03:54.630 --> 03:58.900
Y-Yes, are you eating with the Witch Beatrice?

03:58.900 --> 03:59.480
Yeah.

03:59.930 --> 04:02.050
Th-Then, excuse me.

04:05.340 --> 04:07.980
Yoshimura!

04:09.370 --> 04:13.440
You said eight whole words to Em-chan!

04:13.440 --> 04:14.730
Watanabe-kun...

04:15.170 --> 04:17.700
Eight... You were counting?

04:17.700 --> 04:19.480
Listen.

04:19.480 --> 04:21.650
This is a warning.

04:21.650 --> 04:24.810
If you get any chocolate from Em-chan,

04:24.810 --> 04:29.740
I’ll drag you around the entire school, then exile you
to an island to be crucified, for the rest of your life!

04:30.240 --> 04:31.580
Remember that!

04:34.020 --> 04:35.700
Chocolate?

04:35.700 --> 04:37.800
Oh, yeah. It is close.

04:37.800 --> 04:39.670
That’s right...

04:39.670 --> 04:42.810
It’s coming!

04:44.760 --> 04:46.230
Are you OK?

04:49.300 --> 04:53.850
Yoshimura Mamoru, your days of thinking of me as

04:53.850 --> 04:55.900
a stupid kid in an older grade are numbered.

04:55.900 --> 04:59.110
Shocking new twists in the last episodes!

05:02.270 --> 05:03.950
Valentine’s Day?

05:04.310 --> 05:08.960
What does that have to do with all this chocolate?

05:08.960 --> 05:12.660
Did Saint Valentine like chocolate?

05:12.660 --> 05:15.600
No, it doesn’t matter whether that

05:15.600 --> 05:18.760
Saint Valentine guy liked chocolate or not.

05:18.760 --> 05:20.640
In Japan, on Valentine’s Day,

05:20.640 --> 05:23.880
girls give chocolate to the guys they like

05:23.880 --> 05:26.300
and confess their love to them. It’s stupid.

05:27.210 --> 05:29.240
Confess their love to them...

05:30.470 --> 05:34.180
It’s so stupid, I can play a flute with my nose.

05:34.930 --> 05:35.890
See?

05:35.890 --> 05:37.940
You think so, too, boss?

05:38.490 --> 05:39.980
Really?

05:39.980 --> 05:42.990
In Germany, we exchange presents.

05:42.990 --> 05:46.260
But that’s only between couples and spouses.

05:46.260 --> 05:48.780
I don’t think we confess love to anyone.

05:50.360 --> 05:51.460
Is that so?

05:52.940 --> 05:55.960
Chocolate and confessing...

05:57.920 --> 06:00.110
What’s wrong, Jirou?

06:00.110 --> 06:01.130
Saburou?

06:01.930 --> 06:02.970
Over there...

06:08.330 --> 06:09.910
Witch Beatrice...

06:11.210 --> 06:13.690
She’s smiling.

06:13.690 --> 06:15.890
What’s she reading?

06:15.890 --> 06:17.550
Um...

06:17.550 --> 06:20.490
His heart will be yours!

06:20.490 --> 06:23.590
We’ll tell you how celebrities make their chocolate... Heart.

06:23.590 --> 06:26.540
B-Boss, let’s pretend we didn’t see this!

06:26.540 --> 06:31.450
If she finds out we saw her here,
she’ll beat us to a pulp...

06:31.450 --> 06:32.730
Boss?

06:32.730 --> 06:36.590
If you don’t talk about it until Valentine’s Day itself,

06:36.590 --> 06:39.520
it’ll be more fun for both of you, huh?

06:39.520 --> 06:41.730
Hello, Witch Beatrice.

06:44.320 --> 06:46.860
Wh-What are you doing here?

06:46.860 --> 06:49.470
Shopping with Jirou and Saburou.

06:50.000 --> 06:52.160
But I saw you...

06:52.720 --> 06:55.010
Th-This isn’t...

06:55.010 --> 06:56.760
Don’t get the wrong idea, OK?

06:56.760 --> 06:57.790
Boss! Boss!

06:57.790 --> 07:00.050
Girls like this who are always cold and go,

07:00.050 --> 07:03.420
“I’m not interested in the opposite sex!”

07:03.420 --> 07:05.740
are always the ones with the craziest,

07:05.740 --> 07:10.130
most unspeakable delusions in their heads!

07:10.130 --> 07:11.220
Delusions?

07:11.220 --> 07:12.800
You saw her smirk, right?

07:12.800 --> 07:19.090
I don’t know what kind of pink-colored
delusion she has in her head,

07:19.090 --> 07:21.490
but to secret perverts like her,

07:21.490 --> 07:25.080
Valentine’s is an event of the highest importance, right up there with Christmas!

07:25.080 --> 07:27.820
And she’ll absolutely destroy
anyone who gets in her way—

07:29.510 --> 07:31.060
Why, you...

07:31.060 --> 07:32.620
I can hear you!

07:32.620 --> 07:33.410
Clearly!

07:33.410 --> 07:34.550
Witch Beatrice.

07:34.550 --> 07:37.980
So you were a secret pervert, huh?

07:38.720 --> 07:41.360
Would you like to try death, too?

07:41.360 --> 07:44.510
You should take better care of books.

07:45.190 --> 07:46.780
Y-You’re right.

07:46.780 --> 07:47.940
I’m sorry.

07:47.940 --> 07:52.510
By the way, what is a secret pervert?

07:52.510 --> 07:53.920
I’m going home!

08:03.660 --> 08:04.920
I see.

08:04.920 --> 08:09.980
Valentine’s Day is the one day of the year

08:09.980 --> 08:12.630
for girls to confess their love to boys.

08:16.550 --> 08:19.970
Mamoru has the Witch Beatrice.

08:20.510 --> 08:24.110
I can’t force my way in there.

08:24.780 --> 08:28.090
A battle without honor or humanity... Untenable.

08:37.470 --> 08:41.190
Mamoru’s going to get some from Ayako-san.

08:41.190 --> 08:44.400
I don’t need to make him any...

08:48.740 --> 08:50.880
Mamoru, 1st Grade Mamoru, 8th Grade

08:51.560 --> 08:55.440
Up till last year, I thought it’d be sad if he didn’t get any,

08:55.440 --> 08:57.610
so I made some for him.

08:58.470 --> 09:01.310
He’s grown up...

09:06.590 --> 09:09.750
Valentine’s chocolate from Ayako-san...

09:11.880 --> 09:13.590
I can’t wait.

09:21.300 --> 09:22.270
Now, then...

09:25.110 --> 09:27.140
Valentine’s Planning HQ

09:29.500 --> 09:34.550
Tomorrow will be Ayako and Mamoru-kun’s first Valentine’s.

09:34.550 --> 09:38.020
To make this a special day they’ll remember forever,

09:38.920 --> 09:42.360
we, the Student Council, should do everything we can!

09:44.250 --> 09:45.290
Maicching!

09:46.380 --> 09:48.160
No one asked you to!

09:48.760 --> 09:51.100
It’s too late for that.

09:51.100 --> 09:52.500
Shut up!

09:52.500 --> 09:57.700
It’s better if you don’t talk about it
until the day comes, you know?

09:57.700 --> 09:59.300
And yet, you...

09:59.300 --> 10:04.240
Oh, my. That’s a pretty cute way of thinking, Ayako...

10:04.240 --> 10:05.550
Leave me alone!

10:06.010 --> 10:11.270
But Ayako and Mamoru started dating a long time ago,

10:11.270 --> 10:15.240
so just giving chocolate wouldn’t be enough, would it?

10:15.240 --> 10:18.380
Why not try and make it something
special when you give it to him?

10:18.760 --> 10:22.040
I want a romance, like on TV!

10:22.040 --> 10:26.230
Then you need a rival or two.

10:26.580 --> 10:27.690
Indeed.

10:27.690 --> 10:30.010
Then how about this?

10:30.010 --> 10:32.060
All the female members will give

10:32.060 --> 10:37.910
Mamoru-kun chocolate in the best way that they can think of.

10:38.750 --> 10:46.120
The one who makes his heart pound the most is this year’s Valentine Queen!

10:46.440 --> 10:47.670
I like it.

10:47.670 --> 10:49.070
I really like it.

10:49.070 --> 10:50.970
Hey, what kind of nonsense is this?

10:50.970 --> 10:53.830
Are you scared of losing, Ayako?

10:53.830 --> 10:56.420
No way. I can’t lose!

10:56.700 --> 10:58.060
Then it’s decided.

10:58.800 --> 11:00.130
I’ll be busy!

11:00.620 --> 11:02.060
My heart’s pounding.

11:02.060 --> 11:03.680
Pound! Pound!

11:03.680 --> 11:05.510
You’ll participate, too. Right, Em-chan?

11:06.580 --> 11:09.480
Me, too?

11:09.480 --> 11:11.250
Of course.

11:11.250 --> 11:14.770
You’re a member of the Student Council, too.

11:18.190 --> 11:19.620
Very well.

11:27.110 --> 11:29.960
You knew, right?

11:30.460 --> 11:33.750
That I was going to give you chocolate...

11:36.350 --> 11:37.170
Well...

11:42.360 --> 11:44.160
I was looking forward to it.

11:44.160 --> 11:45.110
Really.

11:46.700 --> 11:48.550
Keep looking forward to it.

11:52.730 --> 11:54.840
W-Witch Beatrice...

11:54.840 --> 11:55.490
Mamoru.

11:56.890 --> 11:59.880
Emelenzia, you’re getting books from the library.

11:59.880 --> 12:00.920
That’s great.

12:00.920 --> 12:02.030
Studying Japanese?

12:02.030 --> 12:05.010
N-No, um...

12:05.010 --> 12:05.870
Excuse me.

12:08.670 --> 12:10.150
What was that?

12:10.150 --> 12:11.330
I don’t know.

12:12.710 --> 12:16.610
I’m just making this for my Student Council activities.

12:16.610 --> 12:19.550
It has no special meaning.

12:28.700 --> 12:30.560
A mysterious taste.

12:31.270 --> 12:33.180
What about this?

12:39.550 --> 12:41.270
This isn’t working.

12:42.480 --> 12:43.570
Boss!

12:43.570 --> 12:45.570
Let’s have some fun!

12:47.020 --> 12:50.540
Come play cards with us, boss...

12:51.100 --> 12:52.720
Jirou, Saburou...

12:52.720 --> 12:55.580
I’m sorry, but I’m busy now.

12:55.580 --> 12:57.820
Busy?

12:57.820 --> 13:00.620
I’ll play cards some other time.

13:00.620 --> 13:01.420
Boss?

13:02.210 --> 13:06.430
Does she not like us anymore?

13:06.430 --> 13:11.700
Saburou, did you realize what she was wearing?

13:11.700 --> 13:12.930
Wearing?

13:13.630 --> 13:17.160
An apron with brown spots on it!

13:17.160 --> 13:19.480
D-Does that mean...

13:19.480 --> 13:20.730
That’s right!

13:20.730 --> 13:22.070
Chocolate!

13:22.070 --> 13:25.950
She’s making Valentine’s chocolate for us!

13:26.420 --> 13:27.870
R-Right!

13:27.870 --> 13:30.250
Tomorrow is Saint Valentine’s Day!

13:30.250 --> 13:31.330
Indeed!

13:31.330 --> 13:37.140
She’s secretly making handmade chocolate for us!

13:34.310 --> 13:42.050
Blessings of the Goddess Upon Mamoru!
Emelenzia Pin-Up

13:37.810 --> 13:42.070
The first Valentine’s Day chocolate I get
in my life, and it’s from the boss...

13:42.540 --> 13:44.200
I’m so glad to be alive!

13:44.200 --> 13:45.920
My life is fulfilled!

13:45.920 --> 13:48.070
I can’t wait for tomorrow!

13:48.070 --> 13:53.210
Come soon, Valentine’s Day!

13:54.130 --> 13:56.440
Valentine’s Day is tomorrow.

13:56.850 --> 13:58.850
There’s no time.

13:58.850 --> 14:02.340
If I could get advice from someone who knows about this...

14:04.650 --> 14:06.530
Knows about this...

14:06.530 --> 14:07.490
That’s it!

14:12.190 --> 14:13.790
Hello hello?

14:17.550 --> 14:24.960
Ayako-san, your chocolate will be mine to get! Get! Get!

14:24.960 --> 14:29.880
Your sweet heart is mine alone!

14:32.180 --> 14:37.870
Who’s bothering me during my talk with Ayako-san?

14:37.870 --> 14:39.610
Jerk.

14:40.150 --> 14:42.430
I-It’s from Maria!

14:42.430 --> 14:44.570
Right, I need to do my job.

14:45.130 --> 14:48.100
Work is work, and Ayako-san is Ayako-san.

14:48.100 --> 14:49.590
Let me see...

14:49.590 --> 14:51.120
<i>I sent the package.</i>

14:51.120 --> 14:56.030
<i>You can use this wonderful object to make Ayako-san’s heart yours for sure.</i>

14:56.030 --> 14:59.050
<i>Until it arrives, the operation is temporarily halted.</i>

14:59.050 --> 15:00.520
<i>Good luck.</i>

15:01.010 --> 15:03.450
No work for a while, huh?

15:03.450 --> 15:04.380
But!

15:06.130 --> 15:10.280
You can use this wonderful object to make Ayako-san’s heart yours for sure?

15:11.810 --> 15:17.760
Then I don’t care if Yoshimura
Mamoru gets some chocolate!

15:17.760 --> 15:20.290
Enjoy it while you can.

15:20.290 --> 15:24.440
Just you wait, Yoshimura Mamoru!

15:24.440 --> 15:27.000
I’ll tear your body and soul and your this and that

15:27.000 --> 15:31.990
into pieces for a Tsuneo special gyoza filling!

15:33.030 --> 15:35.840
Just wait, Yoshimura Mamoru!

15:52.020 --> 15:54.000
Itsumi, good morning.

15:54.000 --> 15:55.060
Good morning.

15:55.590 --> 15:56.900
Thanks for the chocolate.

15:58.860 --> 16:00.830
I just had some extra, OK?

16:01.600 --> 16:03.170
I’ll look forward to it.

16:09.000 --> 16:11.650
Welcome back, master.

16:13.180 --> 16:14.870
What are you doing?

16:14.870 --> 16:16.160
Here!

16:14.950 --> 16:14.990
Love

16:16.160 --> 16:19.910
It’s our sweet, sweet feelings!

16:19.910 --> 16:22.060
Please take it!

16:22.060 --> 16:24.120
Um...

16:27.500 --> 16:28.890
Sempai!

16:28.890 --> 16:31.770
Um, I’m younger than you and in the same class...

16:32.640 --> 16:37.480
And are you two supposed to be
girls with braids and pigtails?

16:37.480 --> 16:39.680
Please take this!

16:41.270 --> 16:43.640
We gave it to him! We gave it to him!

16:47.680 --> 16:48.520
Ayako.

16:48.520 --> 16:50.900
Looks like everyone’s trying all kinds of stuff.

16:51.640 --> 16:53.640
You’re taking it easy, Ayako.

16:54.160 --> 16:57.590
Your beloved Mamoru-kun is everyone’s target right now.

16:58.280 --> 16:59.940
It’s stupid.

17:02.610 --> 17:03.930
Duty-chocolate.

17:03.930 --> 17:05.900
Here you go.

17:17.620 --> 17:19.430
Thank you.

17:22.850 --> 17:25.720
Love, love, love!

17:26.710 --> 17:28.020
What is this?

17:29.710 --> 17:32.320
<i>Chocoball!</i>

17:32.650 --> 17:34.950
E-Even you, Yagi?

17:35.320 --> 17:37.740
I am present!

17:38.530 --> 17:41.430
Hot body! Hot body! Hot body!

17:40.000 --> 17:42.960
Yoshimura Mamoru, Yoshimura Mamoru...

17:42.960 --> 17:45.360
Come to the nurse’s office immediately.

17:46.350 --> 17:47.440
Vice-President?

17:48.580 --> 17:50.670
Excuse me...

17:50.670 --> 17:51.750
Vice-President?

17:52.700 --> 17:57.640
Um, is something wrong?

17:59.890 --> 18:05.470
Once that leaf falls, my short life will come to a close.

18:13.180 --> 18:14.280
Are you OK?!

18:14.280 --> 18:16.050
Yoko, get the camphor!

18:16.050 --> 18:17.130
Right, doctor!

18:17.130 --> 18:18.800
Ana, the IV!

18:18.800 --> 18:20.110
It’s ready, doctor!

18:22.580 --> 18:23.600
Doctor!

18:23.600 --> 18:25.310
Tell me straight!

18:25.800 --> 18:28.080
What is this illness?

18:28.740 --> 18:29.940
It is...

18:29.940 --> 18:31.100
Doctor...

18:32.450 --> 18:35.320
Hereditary Idiotism.

18:35.970 --> 18:38.760
It’s a rare disease that affects one in six billion people!

18:37.540 --> 18:38.760
Then it only affects one!

18:41.930 --> 18:49.360
Unfortunately, there’s nothing else that
modern medicine can do for you.

18:49.360 --> 18:50.980
I understand.

18:50.980 --> 18:56.090
Mamoru-san, will you listen to my last request?

18:56.090 --> 18:57.150
OK.

18:59.450 --> 19:02.030
Th-That’s amazing.

19:02.030 --> 19:04.280
Think of this as me.

19:04.920 --> 19:08.750
Farewell, Mamoru-san!

19:09.730 --> 19:10.570
Wake up!

19:10.570 --> 19:11.760
Open your eyes!

19:12.570 --> 19:13.460
She’s dead!

19:17.610 --> 19:20.020
Ayako-san’s not here yet.

19:20.020 --> 19:20.940
Mamoru...

19:24.100 --> 19:25.380
Emelenzia!

19:26.180 --> 19:27.290
Um...

19:28.070 --> 19:29.010
Take this.

19:30.360 --> 19:33.310
Sorry, my hands are full...

19:35.000 --> 19:36.280
I see.

19:37.970 --> 19:40.440
Then I’ll put it here.

19:40.440 --> 19:43.790
Good. You’re still normal.

19:44.540 --> 19:45.700
Thank you.

19:47.150 --> 19:49.120
Th-Then, goodbye.

19:49.120 --> 19:51.400
Thank you, Emelenzia.

19:51.400 --> 19:52.830
I’ll look forward to it.

19:53.220 --> 19:54.450
Mamoru...

19:58.680 --> 20:00.010
Witch Beatrice!

20:00.540 --> 20:02.800
Th-This isn’t what it looks like.

20:02.800 --> 20:05.320
It’s just part of my student council activities...

20:05.320 --> 20:09.100
Mamoru got lots of duty-chocolate, I guess.

20:11.360 --> 20:16.360
I’m sorry you had to deal with everyone’s stupid game.

20:16.670 --> 20:18.360
Did you make the chocolate OK?

20:19.610 --> 20:23.440
Y-Yes. Goodbye.

20:28.660 --> 20:32.160
You were pretending to be an introverted girl, huh?

20:33.120 --> 20:36.250
It almost looked like it was for real.

20:39.120 --> 20:40.380
For real...

21:03.630 --> 21:04.770
That’s right.

21:04.770 --> 21:05.470
This is for real.

21:06.800 --> 21:10.480
Witch Beatrice... I,

21:12.200 --> 21:15.350
Emelenzia Beatrix Rudiger,

21:16.260 --> 21:20.740
have fallen in love with Yoshimura Mamoru!

22:01.290 --> 22:06.970
My heart is racing and I'm going to give you

22:06.970 --> 22:12.170
This sparkling emotion

22:12.560 --> 22:18.300
The evening color is dyed into this orange shirt

22:18.360 --> 22:23.450
I catch it from behind you and my heart throbbing

22:23.560 --> 22:30.410
It's an everyday thrill just to be with you

22:30.410 --> 22:37.840
I can't say it well enough but thank you

22:37.840 --> 22:43.040
Venus Dream the hidden power

22:43.040 --> 22:49.240
This feeling will change into that power

22:49.240 --> 22:54.360
Power Dream I found what I want to protect

22:54.360 --> 23:00.770
That is your smile and your feelings

23:14.890 --> 23:16.350
Beer Hall.

23:17.680 --> 23:19.210
The promised land.

23:19.960 --> 23:22.760
A paradise where minors are not allowed.

23:22.760 --> 23:25.370
A tomato sandwich that’s just bread with a sliced tomato on it, for 900 yen.

23:25.370 --> 23:27.490
Snacking on nuts like squirrels.

23:27.490 --> 23:29.470
The screams of the crowd echoing everywhere.

23:29.470 --> 23:31.570
The portrait of the founder on the wall!

23:31.570 --> 23:34.950
Middle-aged men looking back upon a lost era and weeping!

23:35.870 --> 23:40.470
Why do I only get the really sad previews?

23:40.170 --> 23:44.000
The Beatrice Disappears?!

23:40.470 --> 23:43.170
Next time: The Beatrice Disappears?!
